WEBVTT

00:00:16.058 --> 00:00:17.560
[dogs yapping]

00:00:26.193 --> 00:00:27.945
[dogs yapping in distance]

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:48.716
[Kublai] <i>Amends must be made</i>
<i>for your father's crime.</i>

00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:49.967
[Marco] I understand.

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:55.889
[dogs barking]

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:05.273
[horses whinnying in distance]

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.198
[whinnying continues]

00:01:39.516 --> 00:01:40.976
[clattering]

00:01:44.813 --> 00:01:47.524
[Kublai] <i>Left to my vice regent, Yusuf,</i>
<i>or myself,</i>

00:01:47.608 --> 00:01:50.443
<i>your father's punishment</i>
<i>would be certain.</i>

00:01:50.527 --> 00:01:53.030
His thief heart would now be still.

00:01:56.408 --> 00:01:58.952
<i>I know the pain</i>
<i>this would cause you.</i>

00:02:04.833 --> 00:02:07.419
[Kublai] I know compassion.

00:02:07.502 --> 00:02:10.297
And you know our customs.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:11.924
Khagan's law.

00:02:12.007 --> 00:02:15.052
You will choose
your father's punishment.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:17.262
And then you shall find sleep.

00:02:20.641 --> 00:02:21.725
[Kublai groans]

00:02:51.755 --> 00:02:53.256
[choking]

00:02:57.302 --> 00:02:58.553
[screaming]

00:03:14.737 --> 00:03:16.279
[coughing weakly]

00:03:52.607 --> 00:03:53.691
Don't kill him!

00:03:53.776 --> 00:03:56.444
We must find out who he serves.

00:03:57.988 --> 00:03:59.197
[screams]

00:04:23.806 --> 00:04:25.808
[theme music playing]

00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:18.753
[Jingim] How is he?

00:06:18.836 --> 00:06:20.713
Poison of the yellow scorpion.

00:06:20.797 --> 00:06:23.841
The healers do not know if he
will survive the night.

00:06:23.926 --> 00:06:27.470
-How many assassins?
-Three.

00:06:27.554 --> 00:06:30.348
Where were his knights?

00:06:30.432 --> 00:06:32.225
Many fell this evening, Jingim.

00:06:32.309 --> 00:06:33.810
Against three assassins?

00:06:39.024 --> 00:06:41.651
I will convene the war assembly.

00:06:48.825 --> 00:06:53.121
Our Great Khan wavers
between this life and the next...

00:06:53.205 --> 00:06:54.789
and we stand here...

00:06:54.872 --> 00:06:58.001
violated within our own walls
and wonder whether we should avenge.

00:06:58.085 --> 00:07:01.379
We do not yet know
who violated us.

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:04.507
[Ahmad] Is there anyone here
aside from my friend Yusuf who cannot--

00:07:04.591 --> 00:07:08.553
[Yusuf] You overstep your office...
my Minister of Finance.

00:07:08.636 --> 00:07:11.181
[Jingim] Our Lord battles
the coward's poison.

00:07:13.558 --> 00:07:15.268
I say this...

00:07:15.352 --> 00:07:19.814
I shall stand for him...
as he has for each of you.

00:07:19.897 --> 00:07:21.316
[Ahmad] Prince...

00:07:21.399 --> 00:07:24.777
we do not know if this
is the tip of Sidao's sword.

00:07:24.861 --> 00:07:28.281
At this very moment, his army
could be descending upon us.

00:07:28.365 --> 00:07:32.910
[Yusuf] We have received
no notice from our outposts

00:07:32.995 --> 00:07:35.413
of any upcoming armies.

00:07:35.497 --> 00:07:37.915
Well, perhaps
they have been eliminated.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.334
[court murmuring assent]

00:07:41.753 --> 00:07:46.424
Thousands of imperial guards...
Mongol knights...

00:07:46.508 --> 00:07:48.676
a moat, deep and wide,

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:51.888
dogs... walls!

00:07:51.972 --> 00:07:55.725
How did this scum
penetrate our defenses?

00:07:57.894 --> 00:08:01.189
Walls and guards,
dogs and moats.

00:08:01.273 --> 00:08:02.315
Prince...

00:08:02.399 --> 00:08:06.944
the answer to the assassins' identity
rests in your question.

00:08:08.196 --> 00:08:11.533
They moved underwater
and through walls...

00:08:11.616 --> 00:08:15.370
sensed only by
the Khan's horses.

00:08:15.453 --> 00:08:19.499
Their tools were
climbing hook and shadow.

00:08:19.582 --> 00:08:24.796
These demons were trained
by the Old Man in the Mountain.

00:08:24.879 --> 00:08:26.923
They were Hashshashin.

00:08:28.008 --> 00:08:29.009
[court murmuring]

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:33.763
The Hashshashin...

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:38.101
were crushed by my uncle Hülegü
long before my birth.

00:08:38.185 --> 00:08:39.436
The Old Man and his martyrs

00:08:39.519 --> 00:08:43.565
are nothing more than phantoms and fables
told to frighten children!

00:08:43.648 --> 00:08:48.070
If they were not Hashshashin,
they were trained in their ways.

00:08:48.153 --> 00:08:53.200
Yusuf is correct in his counsel.
These men are mercenaries.

00:08:53.283 --> 00:08:56.828
They could have been hired
by anyone for any reason.

00:08:56.911 --> 00:09:01.208
Do you advise
I send warriors in search of a myth

00:09:01.291 --> 00:09:05.337
when our true and very real enemy
lies in Xiangyang?

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:09.466
I suggest you open your eyes
to the possibility...

00:09:09.549 --> 00:09:11.926
as your father would.

00:09:12.009 --> 00:09:14.512
How many of our guards were slain?

00:09:14.596 --> 00:09:17.974
Can we afford not to search out
such a potent adversary?

00:09:18.058 --> 00:09:22.687
We can, blind man...
because the Old Man is dead!

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:25.022
Our demons lie south!

00:09:25.107 --> 00:09:27.609
[Marco] With deference, Prince Jingim...

00:09:28.943 --> 00:09:31.028
that may not be true.

00:09:31.113 --> 00:09:34.657
Who allowed you access
to this assembly, Latin?

00:09:34.741 --> 00:09:36.659
Jingim.

00:09:40.497 --> 00:09:41.873
Speak.

00:09:43.583 --> 00:09:44.959
On my journey to Cambulac,

00:09:45.042 --> 00:09:47.087
I passed a village
two weeks ride from here

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:48.921
named Kochkor.

00:09:49.005 --> 00:09:52.884
My guide...
told of a lone way station.

00:09:52.967 --> 00:09:55.720
He was clear that those who
speak the name of Hashshashin...

00:09:55.803 --> 00:09:58.098
were offering their heads
to these assassins

00:09:58.181 --> 00:10:00.433
who are very much alive.

00:10:00.517 --> 00:10:02.269
What is your point?

00:10:02.352 --> 00:10:06.398
If this was the Hashshashin...
we will find them there.

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:10.152
You say you know
where this place rests?

00:10:10.235 --> 00:10:11.861
[Marco] I do.

00:10:11.944 --> 00:10:13.113
Byamba...

00:10:13.196 --> 00:10:16.449
you will ride there with a company
under the banner of the Khan.

00:10:16.533 --> 00:10:18.701
If Master Polo is correct...

00:10:18.785 --> 00:10:22.622
track the assassins and confirm
the Song rebels' complicity.

00:10:22.705 --> 00:10:26.168
In this answer,
the scale of war will be balanced.

00:10:33.216 --> 00:10:36.093
Steady your heart, Marco.
You are of--

00:10:44.519 --> 00:10:46.313
Prince Jingim!

00:10:49.482 --> 00:10:51.734
If a band of Mongolian soldiers
travel as they are,

00:10:51.818 --> 00:10:54.028
the Hashshashin will see danger...

00:10:54.111 --> 00:10:58.991
but... if they ride as escorts
for a merchant searching for poppy,

00:10:59.075 --> 00:11:02.495
the flower by which the Hashshashin
are said to draw their strength...

00:11:02.579 --> 00:11:04.206
It might play a helpful ruse.

00:11:04.289 --> 00:11:08.543
And you, Polo, might get sliced
into fine white meat in the process.

00:11:09.544 --> 00:11:11.254
Prepare your horse.

00:11:11.338 --> 00:11:13.047
Prince...

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:15.633
the Khan and I came to terms
before the attack.

00:11:15.717 --> 00:11:19.512
My father and uncle are to be spared.
I beg you to heed--

00:11:19.596 --> 00:11:24.392
Tonight... your father and uncle
are the least of my concerns.

00:11:24.476 --> 00:11:27.562
I make no promises for tomorrow.

00:11:34.236 --> 00:11:36.571
[Za Bing] An attempt has been made
on the Khan's life.

00:11:38.781 --> 00:11:43.077
-Is he alive?
-Some say yes. Some no.

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:46.873
A party rides
to find those responsible.

00:11:46.956 --> 00:11:50.460
Master Polo is among them.

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:55.298
[Hundred Eyes] I have taught you
to blend with every attack.

00:11:55.382 --> 00:11:56.883
Absorb your opponent.

00:11:56.966 --> 00:12:00.262
-When water is poured into a vessel--
-It becomes the vessel.

00:12:00.345 --> 00:12:04.307
But the Hashshashin
are not common warriors.

00:12:04.391 --> 00:12:09.896
The Old Man trains them to enter
the shadow-self, the demon-self.

00:12:09.979 --> 00:12:12.982
That is their art.

00:12:13.065 --> 00:12:15.693
How does one
absorb such darkness

00:12:15.777 --> 00:12:18.613
and yet return to the light?

00:12:18.696 --> 00:12:21.866
Especially one unsure
of his place in the world?

00:12:23.285 --> 00:12:29.123
If you seek and find the assassins,
you will need to become the vessel.

00:12:29.206 --> 00:12:33.378
If you don't go deep enough,
they will smell you and kill you.

00:12:34.296 --> 00:12:36.130
Go too deep...

00:12:36.213 --> 00:12:39.592
and you will not return
from Eagle's Teaching.

00:12:39.676 --> 00:12:41.052
What marks the balance?

00:12:41.135 --> 00:12:44.055
Certainty of self.

00:12:44.722 --> 00:12:47.559
I do not go for myself, Sifu.

00:12:47.642 --> 00:12:48.935
I go for my father.

00:12:51.228 --> 00:12:53.565
Ride beneath the skyline.

00:12:53.648 --> 00:12:55.608
The Hashshashin
do not wish to be found.

00:12:55.692 --> 00:12:59.028
They will find you.

00:13:07.161 --> 00:13:10.247
[Za Bing] Master Marco...
a moment, please.

00:13:28.725 --> 00:13:33.521
Byamba will travel with a golden tablet.
All gates will open before you.

00:13:33.605 --> 00:13:35.106
Why are you telling me this?

00:13:35.189 --> 00:13:38.067
If the Lord Khan dies
while you're gone...

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:40.194
so does your only advocate.

00:13:40.277 --> 00:13:42.739
Take this tragedy for what it is.

00:13:42.822 --> 00:13:45.533
Opportunity.
Run.

00:14:19.942 --> 00:14:21.193
[indistinct murmuring]

00:14:22.194 --> 00:14:23.905
[Jia Sidao] This...

00:14:24.822 --> 00:14:28.242
is what happens when
we barter with barbarians.

00:14:28.325 --> 00:14:31.829
Cruelty must be met with cruelty.

00:14:31.913 --> 00:14:36.125
We must lay waste to their cities,
their women and children.

00:14:36.208 --> 00:14:40.547
We must drive them back into
the savage hole from which they slid.

00:14:42.339 --> 00:14:43.925
It is time for war.

00:14:45.593 --> 00:14:49.847
[Red Brow] The Emperor's army is yours
to do with as you please...

00:14:49.931 --> 00:14:51.933
my Chancellor.

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:11.453
[Ahmad] You understand
it takes time to gather the troops,

00:15:11.536 --> 00:15:14.581
-to prepare for battle...
-Do you forget who I am?

00:15:16.833 --> 00:15:19.335
I humbly ask that you
give the order to mobilize.

00:15:22.839 --> 00:15:25.341
If you do not prepare to strike...

00:15:25.425 --> 00:15:28.135
worse...
prepare to be struck.

00:15:28.219 --> 00:15:31.681
The Latin may prove Jia Sidao
innocent of the attempt.

00:15:39.063 --> 00:15:41.398
It may.

00:15:41.483 --> 00:15:44.193
Do you not find it odd, Prince...

00:15:44.276 --> 00:15:47.739
that Master Marco spoke so surely
of the assassins' whereabouts?

00:15:47.822 --> 00:15:49.907
So quick to return?

00:15:49.991 --> 00:15:52.577
He does so for the sake of
his own father's head.

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:54.746
And that is my point.

00:15:54.829 --> 00:15:57.832
What would you not do
to realize the dreams of your father?

00:16:00.001 --> 00:16:01.418
Nothing.

00:16:01.503 --> 00:16:05.131
The Khan continues to embrace
this boy we know so little about.

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:10.219
The West is not ignorant
to the Khan's designs.

00:16:10.302 --> 00:16:13.305
Would we not plant rot
within the foundation of their house

00:16:13.389 --> 00:16:15.432
and let it fester
and collapse upon itself?

00:16:15.517 --> 00:16:18.686
You think he travels
to cover transgressions?

00:16:21.022 --> 00:16:22.607
I don't know.

00:16:23.525 --> 00:16:25.610
Perhaps grief
invades my thoughts.

00:16:49.634 --> 00:16:54.055
[Byamba] Has anyone thanked you...
for saving my father's life?

00:16:55.973 --> 00:16:59.476
[Marco] Had you and Hundred Eyes
not arrived, the Khan would be dead...

00:16:59.561 --> 00:17:03.189
as would I.
So... my thanks to you.

00:17:04.649 --> 00:17:06.275
Jingim as Khan...

00:17:07.902 --> 00:17:11.823
-You believe he is not fit?
-I never said that.

00:17:11.906 --> 00:17:13.616
Do you?

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:16.493
This is not my home.
I'm a guest.

00:17:16.578 --> 00:17:18.663
It's not my place to judge my host.

00:17:22.291 --> 00:17:23.918
[Byamba] I hated these as a boy.

00:17:24.001 --> 00:17:26.629
Rotten, sour.

00:17:26.713 --> 00:17:28.297
My mother made me eat them.

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:30.925
She said they kept me healthy.

00:17:31.008 --> 00:17:32.134
And now?

00:17:32.218 --> 00:17:34.303
A superstition before battle.

00:17:34.386 --> 00:17:38.349
Of course, she meant
they were good for my teeth.

00:17:38.432 --> 00:17:41.060
Were you close to her?

00:17:41.143 --> 00:17:42.519
[Byamba] I had to be.

00:17:42.604 --> 00:17:46.107
Son of a consort
is never fully accepted in court.

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:49.526
Will they let me spill blood
on the battlefield? Yes.

00:17:52.113 --> 00:17:53.322
You?

00:17:53.405 --> 00:17:55.617
Were you close to your mother?

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:57.952
She died when I was young.

00:17:58.035 --> 00:18:00.454
I was raised by my aunt.

00:18:00.537 --> 00:18:03.540
I didn't know my father
until three years ago.

00:18:05.126 --> 00:18:07.378
Son of an adventurer.

00:18:08.963 --> 00:18:12.133
Fathers are destined to disappoint sons,
and sons, their fathers.

00:18:12.216 --> 00:18:14.135
The Khan has disappointed you?

00:18:14.761 --> 00:18:17.429
I'm able to find the difference
between the Khan and the man.

00:18:18.765 --> 00:18:20.224
Didn't know that was allowed.

00:18:21.142 --> 00:18:22.894
What is locked behind
the doors of the heart

00:18:22.977 --> 00:18:24.687
is no one's business
but one's own.

00:18:24.771 --> 00:18:27.148
So, let's talk about the man,
and not the Khan.

00:18:27.231 --> 00:18:29.150
Make no mistake...

00:18:29.233 --> 00:18:32.904
even if we meet under the Blue Sky,
I will never open those doors to you.

00:18:33.905 --> 00:18:36.115
And I would never knock.

00:18:37.241 --> 00:18:39.786
You think by doing this,
you can save your father's life?

00:18:41.663 --> 00:18:44.040
I avenge the Khan
and hope he shows him favor.

00:18:45.667 --> 00:18:48.002
The point of all this was to thank you.

00:18:48.085 --> 00:18:51.130
So... thank you.

00:20:02.076 --> 00:20:04.578
Ride swift.
Sidao must know.

00:20:04.661 --> 00:20:08.290
If he does not know that already.
Have you not considered that?

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:14.671
The Mongols will look for spies now,
seek out conspirators.

00:20:14.756 --> 00:20:18.926
You must escape.
Deliver this message yourself.

00:20:20.552 --> 00:20:23.555
If Sidao did not
give the command...

00:20:23.639 --> 00:20:25.682
I must stay.

00:20:25.767 --> 00:20:29.020
My daughter lives or dies
by my decision.

00:20:29.103 --> 00:20:30.604
I remain.

00:21:06.140 --> 00:21:09.226
[Yusuf] Who hired you to kill the Khan?

00:21:09.310 --> 00:21:11.687
I am destined for Paradise.

00:21:11.771 --> 00:21:15.274
That is all I know
and all I will ever claim to know.

00:21:24.575 --> 00:21:26.786
[groaning]

00:21:26.869 --> 00:21:29.371
You don't want to do that.

00:21:31.082 --> 00:21:34.460
If you scream...
you tear your mouth.

00:21:35.878 --> 00:21:39.590
And the more you scream...
the more damage you do to yourself.

00:21:40.632 --> 00:21:43.469
Who hired you?

00:21:43.552 --> 00:21:46.973
I am destined for Paradise.

00:21:47.056 --> 00:21:51.560
That is all I know
and all I will ever claim to know.

00:21:51.643 --> 00:21:52.979
[Yusuf] Very well.

00:21:54.981 --> 00:21:56.273
[Jingim] Anything?

00:21:57.316 --> 00:21:59.986
[sighing]
He may know nothing.

00:22:01.904 --> 00:22:03.865
May know nothing
or knows nothing?

00:22:04.781 --> 00:22:05.992
May.

00:22:06.075 --> 00:22:10.579
Then flay the skin from his bones
until you know.

00:22:23.675 --> 00:22:26.012
You heard the Prince.

00:22:26.095 --> 00:22:31.225
Let us announce to Paradise...
your pending arrival.

00:22:35.479 --> 00:22:36.898
[screaming]

00:22:36.981 --> 00:22:38.857
[screams echoing]

00:22:40.526 --> 00:22:41.777
[door opening]

00:23:13.600 --> 00:23:16.395
How did you come to name your son?

00:23:17.104 --> 00:23:19.648
I did not name Marco.

00:23:21.067 --> 00:23:22.609
His mother had that honor.

00:23:22.693 --> 00:23:24.070
Why?

00:23:25.737 --> 00:23:28.574
I was not present at his birth.

00:23:28.657 --> 00:23:29.741
Where were you?

00:23:31.077 --> 00:23:33.745
In the world.

00:23:36.373 --> 00:23:39.876
So, you abandoned him
before he was even born?

00:23:41.920 --> 00:23:44.881
I was trying to make
a name for my family.

00:23:46.300 --> 00:23:48.594
Although I did not know him...

00:23:48.677 --> 00:23:51.597
everything I have done in my life
has been for him.

00:23:52.514 --> 00:23:55.809
I wanted the world
to know the Polo name.

00:23:55.892 --> 00:23:57.811
So, for legacy?

00:23:57.894 --> 00:23:59.855
Yes.

00:23:59.938 --> 00:24:01.315
[Jingim] His legacy?

00:24:03.484 --> 00:24:04.943
Yes.

00:24:05.861 --> 00:24:08.655
Do you think
that is what he wanted?

00:24:08.739 --> 00:24:11.700
Do you think that was what
he needed from his father?

00:24:11.783 --> 00:24:13.494
Legacy?

00:24:13.577 --> 00:24:16.830
Do you know what your son
asked of me just before he left?

00:24:16.913 --> 00:24:19.833
"Keep them alive until I return.

00:24:19.916 --> 00:24:22.753
Keep them alive."

00:24:22.836 --> 00:24:24.630
Even after you
had abandoned him,

00:24:24.713 --> 00:24:26.382
after he could have died
for your transgressions,

00:24:26.465 --> 00:24:28.759
he was still concerned for you.

00:24:30.802 --> 00:24:32.929
What a fool.

00:24:35.641 --> 00:24:36.975
[Niccolò gasps]

00:24:41.605 --> 00:24:44.150
Never the matter.

00:24:44.233 --> 00:24:46.568
Marco will fall
and you with him.

00:25:31.738 --> 00:25:36.452
All right, my merchant friend.
Let us go peddle your wares.

00:25:37.578 --> 00:25:40.372
We ride below the skyline.

00:25:40.456 --> 00:25:43.959
That is not how we attract
the buyers we need.

00:25:56.472 --> 00:25:58.224
[indistinct chatter]

00:26:09.526 --> 00:26:11.112
[chatter ceases]

00:26:13.739 --> 00:26:15.031
[greeting in Arabic]

00:26:30.547 --> 00:26:31.673
[speaking English]
Done.

00:26:40.056 --> 00:26:43.852
The Chinese say...
"You can name a price for gold...

00:26:43.935 --> 00:26:48.357
but not for the white jade
from the Kingdom of Khotan."

00:26:50.276 --> 00:26:54.446
I do not lie when I say
it's the most precious of all gems...

00:26:54.530 --> 00:26:58.200
and sought by the imperial court.

00:26:58.284 --> 00:27:01.203
What do you wish for this...
white stone?

00:27:02.204 --> 00:27:06.041
The flower that
guides the way to Paradise.

00:27:07.834 --> 00:27:09.336
I wish to speak with the Old Man.

00:27:21.973 --> 00:27:23.016
[Byamba sighs]

00:27:23.099 --> 00:27:25.394
I guess we said something wrong.

00:27:46.415 --> 00:27:47.833
[Jingim] Where are you?

00:27:47.916 --> 00:27:52.379
Wherever he has gone...
he will return.

00:28:06.768 --> 00:28:10.814
I realize now that I had no idea
the pressure one is under...

00:28:10.897 --> 00:28:13.108
turning a son into a man.

00:28:15.236 --> 00:28:18.614
Forget all the citizens in the realm.

00:28:18.697 --> 00:28:22.618
The responsibility parents have
for that one soul.

00:28:23.619 --> 00:28:26.705
It is a great challenge...

00:28:26.788 --> 00:28:29.791
and... a greater honor.

00:28:36.298 --> 00:28:38.384
You are so at peace.

00:28:39.968 --> 00:28:43.889
Peace is found
in the heart of the faithful.

00:28:44.640 --> 00:28:47.017
How can you be
so sure he will wake?

00:28:47.100 --> 00:28:51.230
My faith is rooted in what is next for him
should he not awaken.

00:28:51.313 --> 00:28:54.525
I think too much on this life, Mother...

00:28:54.608 --> 00:28:56.943
to consider what lies beyond.

00:29:16.338 --> 00:29:19.258
[weeping softly]

00:29:29.225 --> 00:29:30.602
May I sit?

00:29:32.646 --> 00:29:34.315
If your intent is on trade.

00:29:34.398 --> 00:29:38.944
It remains unclaimed.
Perhaps your price is too high.

00:29:39.027 --> 00:29:42.781
Everything is open to barter.
What are you offering?

00:29:42.864 --> 00:29:44.908
Opportunity.

00:29:45.826 --> 00:29:46.827
For?

00:29:47.828 --> 00:29:50.997
Leaving through that door
still standing upright.

00:29:54.376 --> 00:29:56.712
And here I was
being so gracious.

00:29:56.795 --> 00:30:00.131
As am I.
I haven't leaned in yet.

00:30:00.674 --> 00:30:01.758
Who are you?

00:30:02.676 --> 00:30:05.053
There are two answers to that question.

00:30:05.136 --> 00:30:06.847
The first is...

00:30:06.930 --> 00:30:09.140
I am the owner of the chair
upon which you sit.

00:30:10.851 --> 00:30:12.060
And the second?

00:30:12.143 --> 00:30:15.481
The last face you will see
before descending into darkness.

00:30:18.734 --> 00:30:19.735
Look around you.

00:30:26.241 --> 00:30:27.368
Over the generations,

00:30:27.451 --> 00:30:31.788
these eaves have shielded the backs
of every culture known to man...

00:30:31.872 --> 00:30:35.834
and as such...
I know man...

00:30:35.917 --> 00:30:38.086
the strong and the weak,

00:30:38.169 --> 00:30:42.257
the bold and the cowardly,
the keen and the foolish...

00:30:42.341 --> 00:30:45.636
and you are strong... bold...

00:30:45.719 --> 00:30:50.098
and far from foolish enough
to track this trouble across my floor...

00:30:50.181 --> 00:30:53.935
unless you have convinced yourselves
through conditioning...

00:30:54.019 --> 00:30:56.229
that no harm will befall you.

00:30:57.814 --> 00:30:59.065
Show me.

00:31:09.284 --> 00:31:12.704
The Khan of Khans
grants the golden tablet to poppy dealers?

00:31:12.788 --> 00:31:14.289
No...

00:31:14.373 --> 00:31:17.418
a bureaucrat in the Secretariat
with a liking for hashish.

00:31:17.501 --> 00:31:19.795
I do not carry
the product you seek.

00:31:19.878 --> 00:31:22.631
[scoffs] Then what kind of seller are you?

00:31:23.799 --> 00:31:26.217
I am the man in the middle.

00:31:26.301 --> 00:31:28.637
We want the Gatekeeper of Paradise.

00:31:29.555 --> 00:31:31.723
That man...

00:31:31.807 --> 00:31:33.600
is far too deadly.

00:31:35.936 --> 00:31:37.270
Let us weigh the stakes.

00:31:39.147 --> 00:31:41.066
I misread you.

00:31:42.358 --> 00:31:44.027
You are a fool.

00:32:07.175 --> 00:32:08.677
[knock on door]

00:32:13.098 --> 00:32:14.641
Continue.

00:32:31.617 --> 00:32:33.577
[Jingim] Sidao slaughtered
his ambassadors.

00:32:34.495 --> 00:32:35.496
My Prince?

00:32:35.579 --> 00:32:39.249
The Song ambassadors
we parleyed with...

00:32:39.332 --> 00:32:40.375
the warriors we freed,

00:32:40.459 --> 00:32:42.628
they were all butchered
returning to Xiangyang.

00:32:42.711 --> 00:32:47.048
Sidao lays the blame at our doorstep.
His army prepares for battle.

00:32:48.341 --> 00:32:50.636
Diplomacy is dead.

00:32:52.846 --> 00:32:55.223
You negotiated a true peace.

00:32:55.306 --> 00:32:56.683
Empress Dowager would've embraced it.

00:32:56.767 --> 00:33:00.395
Sidao has rejected our truce
with steel and blood.

00:33:02.022 --> 00:33:03.189
This is a good sign.

00:33:03.273 --> 00:33:04.733
Find for me the good in this.

00:33:04.816 --> 00:33:06.527
We have clarity of the inevitable.

00:33:06.610 --> 00:33:09.112
We know now
Xiangyang is divided.

00:33:09.195 --> 00:33:13.033
War is how this will end...
and now is a time to strike.

00:33:13.116 --> 00:33:15.786
We do not know
if Sidao moved against my father.

00:33:15.869 --> 00:33:18.329
We do not know if the Song
mobilize to attack or to defend.

00:33:18.413 --> 00:33:20.165
-We know nothing--
-[Ahmad] My Prince!

00:33:20.248 --> 00:33:24.377
My brother, yes, we need not march,
but... at least marshal our forces.

00:33:24.460 --> 00:33:26.379
We must prepare.

00:33:26.462 --> 00:33:29.049
In this, you must not fail.

00:33:29.132 --> 00:33:30.592
Gather your generals.

00:33:30.676 --> 00:33:31.802
Speak to them as warriors

00:33:31.885 --> 00:33:34.805
and they will follow you
past the gates of death.

00:33:34.888 --> 00:33:36.807
As they followed me at Wuchang?

00:33:36.890 --> 00:33:38.684
The army respects you.

00:33:38.767 --> 00:33:40.894
You attacked at Wuchang
against greater numbers.

00:33:40.977 --> 00:33:42.437
And I failed.

00:33:42.521 --> 00:33:45.481
But only while daring greatly.

00:33:45.566 --> 00:33:48.401
You advanced on a larger army
as Genghis would.

00:33:49.570 --> 00:33:52.113
Soldiers understand
losing is part of the journey...

00:33:52.197 --> 00:33:55.617
so long as their leader
does not believe it the destination.

00:33:55.701 --> 00:33:57.243
Your father understands this.

00:33:58.078 --> 00:33:59.412
He did not act as if he did.

00:33:59.495 --> 00:34:01.832
Would you have him savor defeat?

00:34:03.792 --> 00:34:06.211
No...

00:34:06.294 --> 00:34:08.797
but to speak as you do...

00:34:08.880 --> 00:34:10.173
once.

00:34:10.256 --> 00:34:12.508
He feels as I do...

00:34:12.593 --> 00:34:15.554
and he would say it now,
had he voice.

00:34:15.637 --> 00:34:18.431
Lend him your voice.

00:34:18.514 --> 00:34:22.853
Speak for Father now...
and command as Khan.

00:34:44.625 --> 00:34:47.418
[Byamba] Who is the
Old Man in the Mountain?

00:34:47.502 --> 00:34:50.672
[Sabbah] You certainly
are not fond of your throat, are you?

00:34:50.756 --> 00:34:53.174
You will not speak his name...

00:34:53.258 --> 00:34:58.013
and once I have taken you to him...
you will never return again.

00:34:58.096 --> 00:35:02.684
We have no reason to...
unless we are invited by you.

00:35:02.768 --> 00:35:04.185
[Sabbah laughs]

00:35:04.269 --> 00:35:06.479
You learn well, Europa.

00:35:10.984 --> 00:35:12.736
Which way?

00:35:12.819 --> 00:35:14.988
To Eagle's Teaching?

00:35:15.906 --> 00:35:19.325
One can only enter through Paradise.

00:35:19.409 --> 00:35:21.036
[eagle screeching]

00:35:25.498 --> 00:35:27.250
[Sabbah] A secret order

00:35:27.333 --> 00:35:30.295
formed at the time
of the First Crusade.

00:35:30.378 --> 00:35:33.173
The Old Man has
always lived among them...

00:35:33.256 --> 00:35:35.967
granting access to Paradise.

00:35:38.762 --> 00:35:40.471
Is he a magic man?

00:35:40.555 --> 00:35:42.182
He is a holy man.

00:35:42.265 --> 00:35:45.936
I think you trade
in black market fables.

00:35:46.019 --> 00:35:48.604
That's what I think.

00:35:48.689 --> 00:35:53.318
You have a much more genteel personality
than your friend.

00:35:53.401 --> 00:35:57.656
It takes time...
but he will soften... eventually.

00:35:57.739 --> 00:35:59.700
I will not.

00:35:59.783 --> 00:36:00.992
[chuckles]

00:36:18.009 --> 00:36:20.095
Byamba, do you see?

00:36:27.435 --> 00:36:29.813
It is not the sun.

00:36:29.896 --> 00:36:35.485
It's a... golden passage...
into the heavens.

00:36:35.568 --> 00:36:38.905
Marvelous description.

00:36:50.792 --> 00:36:52.711
Are they watching us now?

00:36:52.794 --> 00:36:56.506
They have been watching you
since before we exchanged names.

00:40:14.245 --> 00:40:15.621
You are the Old Man.

00:40:15.705 --> 00:40:19.750
Some call me by that name, yes...

00:40:19.834 --> 00:40:25.215
but I've lived more lives
than any man under the sun...

00:40:25.298 --> 00:40:29.844
and will live many more
beyond this day.

00:40:29.928 --> 00:40:34.265
[Marco] And this... is a place
of hidden knowledge?

00:40:34.349 --> 00:40:38.144
[Old Man] This is a place of freedom...

00:40:38.228 --> 00:40:43.191
where no one questions who you are,
where you come from,

00:40:43.274 --> 00:40:45.944
what tongue you speak.

00:40:46.027 --> 00:40:50.073
You are welcome
as you are, son.

00:40:50.156 --> 00:40:53.784
I can return you to Paradise
if you wish.

00:40:53.868 --> 00:40:55.536
What have you done
with our men?

00:40:56.204 --> 00:40:59.415
It is their choice to stay or leave.

00:40:59.499 --> 00:41:01.917
Some prefer to stay.

00:41:02.002 --> 00:41:05.130
So, tell me, Marco Polo...

00:41:05.213 --> 00:41:07.007
why did you come?

00:41:07.673 --> 00:41:10.551
To discover or to destroy?

00:41:10.635 --> 00:41:13.096
Give me my men
and I will give you the answer.

00:41:15.848 --> 00:41:18.351
Discovery.

00:41:18.434 --> 00:41:21.187
I came to learn
who hired your assassins.

00:41:22.688 --> 00:41:24.315
Offer me this knowledge...

00:41:24.399 --> 00:41:28.236
and you will gain favor
with the most powerful man on earth.

00:41:28.319 --> 00:41:30.405
The Great Khan lives, then.

00:41:30.488 --> 00:41:32.823
And your disciples do not.

00:41:35.118 --> 00:41:36.869
Kill us...

00:41:37.996 --> 00:41:41.791
and the Khan will finish
what his ancestors began.

00:41:41.874 --> 00:41:44.544
He must find us first.

00:41:44.627 --> 00:41:46.421
[Marco] If I could find you...

00:41:47.172 --> 00:41:50.091
the Mongols will find you.

00:41:50.175 --> 00:41:54.012
They will rain fire,
black out the sun.

00:41:54.095 --> 00:41:57.223
You will have no peace,
no sanctuary...

00:41:57.307 --> 00:42:00.685
and my Great Khan
will prove you mortal.

00:42:00.768 --> 00:42:06.274
You are precisely
the kind of young man I welcome here.

00:42:07.900 --> 00:42:10.070
Clever... spirited...

00:42:10.153 --> 00:42:15.700
and deserving of Paradise,
however you define it.

00:42:22.998 --> 00:42:27.753
We do not deal in name and faces...

00:42:29.297 --> 00:42:32.007
only in coin and anonymity.

00:42:32.092 --> 00:42:35.095
And how much coin
did the Song Chancellor give you?

00:42:35.845 --> 00:42:41.601
The hand that dropped the purse
lives far closer to home, son.

00:42:53.113 --> 00:42:55.781
[Old Man] Safe journey, Marco Polo.

00:42:57.032 --> 00:42:58.826
[man groaning weakly]

00:43:14.049 --> 00:43:17.095
How many more days and nights
will this continue?

00:43:17.178 --> 00:43:18.221
[Yusuf sighs]

00:43:18.304 --> 00:43:22.433
What do you hope to get from a man...
we know can give you nothing?

00:43:24.102 --> 00:43:26.521
Nothing but hope...

00:43:26.604 --> 00:43:30.150
that he might give me
anything to use to avoid your war.

00:43:33.111 --> 00:43:37.198
You and I are not Mongols.
We are servants.

00:43:37.282 --> 00:43:38.783
[chuckles]
This is not my war.

00:43:38.866 --> 00:43:41.702
Yet you fight for it so rabidly.

00:43:41.786 --> 00:43:44.038
And you so rabidly against it.

00:43:44.122 --> 00:43:45.206
Why?

00:43:46.124 --> 00:43:49.544
The rebels have not once
set foot outside Xiangyang...

00:43:49.627 --> 00:43:51.879
for any purpose
but trade and travel.

00:43:51.962 --> 00:43:53.256
They stage raids

00:43:53.339 --> 00:43:55.508
and they attack my collectors
as they ride the realm.

00:43:55.591 --> 00:44:00.138
The price of doing business
in a treacherous world.

00:44:00.221 --> 00:44:04.475
Their army hides behind walls
for fear of extermination,

00:44:04.559 --> 00:44:08.396
a wall that has
defied and denied us for 70 years.

00:44:08.479 --> 00:44:11.566
Our men will die for no reason...

00:44:11.649 --> 00:44:14.985
save the ego of the man
ordering the breach.

00:44:16.362 --> 00:44:18.281
Ego...

00:44:18.364 --> 00:44:20.991
not armies, destroys empires.

00:44:22.452 --> 00:44:26.789
Our Khan is chased to the wall
by the ghost of Genghis.

00:44:30.460 --> 00:44:32.587
Our Khan still breathes.

00:44:34.004 --> 00:44:35.506
[man groaning]

00:44:38.593 --> 00:44:41.679
[Yusuf] The man will soon
join his brothers...

00:44:41.762 --> 00:44:45.015
and if you have your way, Ahmad...

00:44:45.099 --> 00:44:47.185
so shall we all.

00:44:53.190 --> 00:44:54.400
[sighs]

00:45:07.913 --> 00:45:10.791
[Jia Sidao] Word from my sister.

00:45:10.875 --> 00:45:14.254
Someone has attempted
to kill the barbarian king.

00:45:21.051 --> 00:45:23.679
We're not alone
in our loathing of the Khan.

00:45:28.726 --> 00:45:32.229
The devil sleeps soundly tonight.

00:45:32.313 --> 00:45:33.814
It displeases me.

00:45:34.732 --> 00:45:38.319
But he will survive.
He's fated to do so.

00:45:46.076 --> 00:45:49.830
Someone has foolishly
stepped upon my path...

00:45:49.914 --> 00:45:53.334
endeavoring to forge a tributary
and force me down it.

00:45:54.251 --> 00:45:56.587
The Khan will awaken.

00:45:56.671 --> 00:45:59.590
The Mongol horde
will descend upon my wall...

00:45:59.674 --> 00:46:01.592
and my blade...

00:46:01.676 --> 00:46:05.095
will find its destiny
in the barbarian's heart.

00:46:10.560 --> 00:46:13.521
You are the only one
I might speak freely to...

00:46:13.604 --> 00:46:15.898
the only one I can trust.

00:46:20.361 --> 00:46:23.448
It makes me happy
to know I have this with you.

00:46:27.493 --> 00:46:29.704
[Byamba] This is
my father's private quarters.

00:46:29.787 --> 00:46:32.915
The traitor
is someone in his service...

00:46:32.998 --> 00:46:34.291
someone he trusts.

00:46:35.209 --> 00:46:37.337
I may know the hand
that made these marks.

00:46:37.420 --> 00:46:38.713
Whose hand?

00:46:39.464 --> 00:46:41.674
Someone who has passed on.

00:46:57.398 --> 00:46:59.316
Two months to the Hindu Kush.

00:46:59.400 --> 00:47:02.820
Up, down, give or take a year
and you're in Venice.

00:47:02.903 --> 00:47:06.073
You have time
before the snows fall.

00:47:06.156 --> 00:47:08.618
You were killed by the Hashshashin.

00:47:10.536 --> 00:47:11.829
You would let me go?

00:47:11.912 --> 00:47:13.873
You are a guest
in someone else's home.

00:47:13.956 --> 00:47:15.708
You should leave when you wish.

00:47:15.791 --> 00:47:19.169
Upon our return, your host may be gone
and you would be friendless.

00:47:19.253 --> 00:47:21.381
Are we not now friends, Byamba?

00:47:21.464 --> 00:47:23.758
I cannot save you in Cambulac.

00:47:31.348 --> 00:47:33.100
Would you defy the Khan?

00:47:33.183 --> 00:47:34.351
[Byamba] No...

00:47:34.435 --> 00:47:36.771
but this is my home...

00:47:36.854 --> 00:47:40.107
and if someone were keeping me from it,
I would kill to return.

00:47:43.318 --> 00:47:44.695
[sighing]

00:48:27.905 --> 00:48:29.323
[Ahmad] Jingim!

00:48:29.406 --> 00:48:30.991
Our father wakes.

00:48:33.494 --> 00:48:35.329
Welcome news, brother.

00:48:36.497 --> 00:48:38.082
I will join him.

00:49:13.075 --> 00:49:15.285
My head is weak.

00:49:16.537 --> 00:49:18.247
It will strengthen.

00:49:19.540 --> 00:49:22.459
Perhaps it's best if it did not.

00:49:22.543 --> 00:49:25.755
My son seems to have
that side well under control.

00:49:27.172 --> 00:49:30.467
You could easily
have rushed into war.

00:49:30.551 --> 00:49:33.387
Few would have
questioned the move.

00:49:33.470 --> 00:49:35.472
Your control guided you.

00:49:36.974 --> 00:49:39.476
I never felt in control, Sire.

00:49:39.560 --> 00:49:40.978
[chuckling]

00:49:46.692 --> 00:49:48.528
Curse of the Khanate.

00:49:49.904 --> 00:49:52.114
The kingdom must know
that I'm alive and well

00:49:52.197 --> 00:49:54.324
before we march into war.

00:49:54.408 --> 00:49:56.619
Get me to my throne.

00:49:58.328 --> 00:49:59.371
[grunting]

00:50:00.581 --> 00:50:01.666
[chuckles]

00:50:36.992 --> 00:50:38.994
[horses approaching]

00:50:59.431 --> 00:51:01.601
[Byamba] It has details
of your inner chamber

00:51:01.684 --> 00:51:03.853
few would know, Lord Khan.

00:51:03.936 --> 00:51:07.397
I spend my Khanate
embracing enemy cultures.

00:51:07.481 --> 00:51:11.902
Treachery grows well in
the fertile soil of contempt I've tilled.

00:51:11.986 --> 00:51:13.403
Who else knows of this map?

00:51:13.487 --> 00:51:17.199
No one... but Byamba,
myself, and its creator.

00:51:17.282 --> 00:51:18.909
Circle must remain small.

00:51:18.993 --> 00:51:20.244
What of Jingim?

00:51:21.203 --> 00:51:24.123
I do not wish to burden him as of yet.

00:51:24.206 --> 00:51:26.000
You say you recognize the scratch?

00:51:26.917 --> 00:51:30.587
I wish to confirm this belief
before I tarnish his name any further.

00:51:33.090 --> 00:51:35.425
I trust you both to do so.

00:51:35.509 --> 00:51:38.846
Follow the map, where it leads,
under my aegis.

00:51:38.929 --> 00:51:40.931
Bring answers back to your Khan.

00:51:51.859 --> 00:51:53.736
Hold, Latin.

00:52:01.118 --> 00:52:05.580
You defended me courageously...
even in the face of death.

00:52:06.498 --> 00:52:08.250
I was one of many...

00:52:08.333 --> 00:52:11.045
and it pleases me greatly
to return and find you well.

00:52:11.128 --> 00:52:12.838
Mmm.

00:52:12.922 --> 00:52:15.049
Have you made your decision...

00:52:15.132 --> 00:52:17.384
regarding the fate
of your father and uncle?

00:52:18.302 --> 00:52:20.971
No, Lord Kublai.

00:52:21.055 --> 00:52:23.640
I thought--
I hoped...

00:52:24.850 --> 00:52:26.560
you might pardon them.

00:52:27.269 --> 00:52:29.063
Is pardon punishment?

00:52:30.480 --> 00:52:34.443
I wished...
you would spare them.

00:52:35.277 --> 00:52:37.112
Why would I do that?

00:52:40.908 --> 00:52:42.201
[Maffeo praying in Latin]

